ClarityFi – Product Requirements Document (Stakeholder Ready)
Version 1.0 | June 2026 | Personal Finance / FinTech
1. Executive Summary
ClarityFi is a personal finance clarity platform designed for everyday consumers who generate abundant financial data but lack actionable insight. The product combines automated spend intelligence, smart expense splitting, and financial decision support into a single experience.
2. Market Opportunity
India has over 350M monthly UPI users. Consumers make dozens of transactions every month yet struggle to understand spending behavior, manage shared expenses, and evaluate financial products. Existing solutions address only fragments of the problem.
3. Problem Statement
Users are financially aware but financially blind. They know money leaves their accounts but cannot easily determine where it goes, whether they are overspending, or if financial decisions are optimal.
4. Product Vision
Help every user understand, manage, and act on their money with confidence through simple, transparent financial intelligence.
5. Product Goals
• Improve spending awareness
• Reduce friction in shared expense management
• Increase confidence in financial decisions
• Create recurring engagement through personalized insights
6. Success Metrics
North Star Metric: Monthly Active Users who act on a financial insight.

Supporting Metrics:
• 60%+ users identify a new spending pattern
• 40%+ Day-30 retention
• 25%+ Day-90 retention
• 35%+ users create split groups
• NPS > 40
7. User Personas
Persona 1: Riya – Overwhelmed Earner
Persona 2: Arjun – Reluctant Splitter
Persona 3: Meera – Confused Decision Maker

Each persona represents a distinct pain point around spending visibility, group expenses, and financial decision-making.
8. Jobs To Be Done (JTBD)
When I spend money every day, I want to know where it goes so that I can make better decisions.
When I share expenses with others, I want settlements to happen automatically so that awkward conversations are avoided.
When I evaluate an EMI or insurance plan, I want plain-language explanations so that I can choose confidently.
9. User Research Insights
Common themes:
• Users underestimate discretionary spending.
• Shared expense tracking is highly manual.
• Financial products are perceived as confusing.
• Users prefer automated solutions over manual bookkeeping.
10. Product Scope (MVP)
Feature 1: Spend Clarity Dashboard
Feature 2: Smart Expense Splitter
Feature 3: Financial Decision Explainer
11. Detailed Feature Requirements
Spend Dashboard:
- SMS transaction parsing
- Auto categorization
- Trend analysis
- Weekly and monthly insights

Expense Splitter:
- Group creation
- Equal/custom splits
- Settlement optimization
- UPI payment initiation

Decision Explainer:
- EMI evaluator
- Insurance evaluator
- Hidden fee detection
- Recommendation engine
12. User Stories & Acceptance Criteria
As a user, I want to see categorized spending so that I understand where my money goes.
Acceptance: Transactions categorized automatically with >85% accuracy.

As a user, I want to split expenses with friends so that balances are calculated automatically.
Acceptance: System generates settlement recommendations.

As a user, I want EMI offers explained clearly.
Acceptance: System displays total cost and hidden charges.
