• AES-256 encryption
• TLS 1.3 data transmission
• User-controlled data deletion
• No sale of transaction data
17. Analytics & Event Tracking
Track:
- Onboarding completion
- SMS permission acceptance
- Dashboard engagement
- Split group creation
- Settlement completion
- EMI evaluations
- Weekly active users
18. Competitive Analysis
Splitwise: Strong splitting, weak spend intelligence.
CRED: Premium UX, limited financial visibility.
Money View/Walnut: Tracking-focused, limited decision support.

Differentiator: Unified spending, splitting, and decision intelligence.
19. Risks & Mitigations
Permission denial → Manual entry fallback
Low retention → Insight-driven engagement
Parsing failures → Continuous rule updates
Trust concerns → Privacy-first architecture
20. Launch Strategy
Pilot launch with 200–500 users in Bengaluru and Pune.
Measure activation, retention, and insight engagement.
Iterate before wider rollout.
21. Roadmap
Phase 1: Dashboard + SMS Parsing + Splitter
Phase 2: Decision Intelligence + UPI Settlements
Phase 3: Account Aggregation + Family Finance
Phase 4: Premium Analytics & Monetization
